      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Auto mode is now the default in Claude Code",
      "url": "https://claude.com/blog/auto-mode-default-in-claude-code",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49239021",
      "score": 168,
      "comments": 148,
      "author": "sbehere",
      "published": "2026-08-10T03:50:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Anthropic's terminal agent now autonomously executes bash commands and edits files without requiring step-by-step user confirmation.",
        "The shift highlights an industry transition toward agentic friction-free workflows, prioritizing execution speed over explicit human-in-the-loop verification.",
        "Engineers and security teams using AI CLI tools must enforce strict sandboxing to prevent unintended or destructive bash execution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Undo/redo systems and collaborative editing (2024)",
      "url": "https://dev.to/isaachagoel/you-dont-know-undoredo-4hol",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/wew6tz",
      "score": 2,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "fractalbeauty",
      "published": "2026-08-10T03:40:35Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Decouple local user undo stacks from global history using CRDTs (e.g., Yjs, Automerge) or Operational Transformation to track individual operation intent.",
        "Implementing selective undo requires operational inversion, transforming local inverted operations against concurrent remote edits without reordering global document state.",
        "Use operation-based logs with tombstone tracking rather than full state snapshots to safely invert historical actions in real-time multi-user environments."
      ]
    },
    {
